## Original Content
Это увеличит время работы заправок и количество заправленных машин в день, отметил глава региона Игорь Бабушкин

## Summary
The Astrakhan region is reducing fuel allocation to 30 liters per person. This measure aims to increase gas station efficiency by extending working hours and refueling more cars daily. The regional head, Igor Babushkin, announced this change.

## Key Points
- Fuel allocation reduced to 30 liters per person in Astrakhan region.
- Goal is to increase gas station working time.
- Expected to boost daily car refueling numbers.
- Decision announced by regional head Igor Babushkin.
- Part of fuel distribution management strategy.


